---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About — Last Ride Registry"
  description="Why the registry exists, how cases are published and corrected, and what comes next: tracing what happened to the drivers, case by case."
  current="/about"
>
  <!-- ============ mission ============ -->
  <section id="mission" aria-label="Why this exists">
    <div class="section" style="padding-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Why this exists</p>
      <h2>The federal record stops at the death</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        NHTSA counts every cyclist killed by a driver. No national database records whether
        the driver was charged, convicted, or never heard from again. This registry exists so
        the answer is public: every death mapped and downloadable, and case by case, what came
        after.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ editorial policy ============ -->
  <section id="editorial" aria-label="Editorial policy">
    <div class="section" style="padding-top: 0; padding-bottom: 3rem;">
      <p class="kicker">How we publish</p>
      <h2>Facts only, cited, correctable</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every named case traces to a published news report or a court record, linked inline.
        Drivers are named only once formally charged. Legal status is always dated, never
        final. Families can request corrections or removal — the full policy is public
        in&#32;<a href="https://github.com/f-mac/lastrideregistry/blob/main/EDITORIAL.md">EDITORIAL.md</a>,
        and every change is visible in the repository history.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ roadmap ============ -->
  <section id="next" aria-label="What comes next">
    <div class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <p class="kicker">What comes next</p>
      <h2>The question the federal data never answers: what happened to the driver?</h2>
      <div class="roadmap">
        <div class="step now">
          <span class="tag">Now — v1</span>
          <h3>The open registry</h3>
          <p>Every death since 2010, mapped and downloadable, with recent cases curated by hand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="tag">Next — v2</span>
          <h3>Verified accountability</h3>
          <p>
            For every 2023 hit-and-run death — roughly 275 cases, old enough that prosecutions
            have resolved — we will trace each outcome through court records rather than news
            coverage, and publish it as open data, case by case, with citations.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="tag">Then — v3</span>
          <h3>Every year, every case</h3>
          <p>
            Expand cohort by cohort until "was the driver charged?" has a public answer for
            every cyclist killed in America — and a correction channel so families and local
            advocates can keep it honest.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
